  "lineage": "Circumpolar Sápmi vocal art across northern Norway, Sweden, Finland and the Kola Peninsula, documented from the 17th-century missionary suppression records and revived from the 1960s-70s by Nils-Aslak Valkeapää and later Mari Boine — short cyclic melodic cells of narrow ambitus repeated with subtle variation, non-lexical vocables (loi-la-loi) carrying more weight than text, glottal catches and pulsing chest attacks, no fixed metric frame, historically unaccompanied though the noaidi's oval frame drum survives in ritual and revival use.",
